+# Phase 6 BC-3a2 session (grok)
+
+Worker: grok
+Run: BC-3a2 (repair of quota-blocked Gemini BC-3a)
+Findings: BD-01 (build-time tickets at raw and Index), BD-03 (ledger-fenced
+reconstruction), BD-05 (unrelated sidecar edit), BD-06 (pre-materialization
+corpus bytes)
+Base: `fc544f2` on `cc/living-library` (`control-room/5aca8450-af7-grok`),
+which already includes BC-3b and BC-3c.
+Do not commit. Astra verifies and integrates before BD-2.
+
+## Status
+
+Complete. Five assigned reproductions pass. Full BD file 14/14. Companion
+suites named in `PHASE6-BC3-BRIEF-2026-09-08.md` pass. Gemini's unapplied
+ten-line patch was not used. No commit.
+
+## Repair
+
+- **BD-01.** `Index.publish_media_snapshot` refuses an omitted ticket
+  (`invalid_request` / `publication_ticket_required`) and does not mint.
+  Raw `publish_transcript` will not mint a new base for a never-published
+  content-bearing snapshot after a ledger exists. Owning callers already
+  carry a ticket from `begin_publication` (podcasts, capture). BC-2 Index
+  replacements use `_index_publish`; content-bearing raw replacements after
+  a ledger use `_owned_publish`. `_seed_index` materializes without a
+  ledger so BD-01's Index setup can still publish B through the frozen
+  raw helper.
+- **BD-03.** `rebuild_item` takes `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, reads the publication
+  ledger, and refuses a sidecar whose media revision is not the ledger
+  current (and a disk sidecar that disagrees with that current) before any
+  DB write.
+- **BD-05.** `PublicationTicket` snapshots non-owned sidecar keys at mint
+  time. Intervening edits of those keys, and keys that exist only on disk,
+  are merged onto the published carrier before replacement. A final byte
+  recheck refuses a further change.
+- **BD-06.** The corpus-edit guard no longer requires a current media
+  block. User-edited pre-materialization bytes whose digest is not the
+  recorded current corpus refuse `revision_unavailable` before any write.
+
+Ticketless raw calls remain only for a first fenced publication, an
+idempotent current target, a ledger-history `superseded_snapshot` refusal,
+and the frozen evaluation empty-replacement helper (no cues or chapters).
+Production Index publication always requires the build-time ticket.
+
+## Commands and observed counts
+
+Interpreter: `C:\Python314\python.exe` (3.14.6). Worktree cwd. PowerShell.
+
+Environment: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, `PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1`,
+`PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` unset, `librarian_apply_enabled`
+untouched. `PYTHONPATH` is the worktree plus the resolved installed
+user-site (`C:\Users\hello\AppData\Roaming\Python\Python314\site-packages`
+and its `win32` / `win32\lib` / `pythonwin` subdirs). Disposable roots
+under worktree `.bc3a2-scratch\` (`TEMP`/`TMP`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `APPDATA`,
+`USERPROFILE`/`HOME`); removed after the runs. Phase 3 also
+`PHASE3_REQUIRE_IMPLEMENTATION=1`. No model, helper, port 5179, live
+index, or paid API.
